    "results": [
      {
        "obligationId": "scenario%3Afile-owner-without-destination-write-grant::entry%3Apost-process-file",
        "conclusion": "source_supported_failure",
        "explanation": "source_supported_failure. At the declared POST /process/file entry, authentication binds a verified user, and the non-admin branch authorizes access only to the supplied source file by looking it up with both file_id and user.id. The caller-supplied collection_name is then copied into the destination binding and passed to save_docs_to_vector_db with add=True whenever a collection name was supplied. For an existing collection, add=True bypasses the helper's non-add early return, and the protected effect is VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert into that named collection. No destination ownership or explicit write-grant check is visible on this path. The separately supplied collection-access validator could raise 403 for denied collections, but the declared process_file path does not invoke it. Thus source-file ownership is treated as sufficient to reach a write to the independently selected destination, contrary to the accepted destination-write policy. The write path requires BYPASS_EMBEDDING_AND_RETRIEVAL to be false and ordinary processing to succeed; that deployment/runtime state is not established by the fixed source, but it is not a missing authorization binding and does not change the source-visible absence of target-specific authorization.",
        "facts": {
          "entry": [
            {
              "statement": "The declared entry is POST /process/file, taking ProcessFileForm and requiring a verified user dependency.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1546,
                  "endLine": 1552,
                  "quote": "@router.post('/process/file')\nasync def process_file(\n    request: Request,\n    form_data: ProcessFileForm,\n    user=Depends(get_verified_user),\n    db: AsyncSession = Depends(get_async_session),\n):"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "binding": [
            {
              "statement": "The route assigns the destination collection directly from form_data.collection_name, defaulting to a file-specific collection only when the caller omitted it.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1564,
                  "endLine": 1569,
                  "quote": "    if file:\n        try:\n            collection_name = form_data.collection_name\n\n            if collection_name is None:\n                collection_name = f'file-{file.id}'"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "For a non-admin, the route retrieves the source file by both the submitted file identifier and the authenticated user's identifier, binding authorization to source-file ownership; the separate admin branch omits that ownership restriction.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1559,
                  "endLine": 1563,
                  "quote": "    if user.role == 'admin':\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id(form_data.file_id, db=db)\n    else:\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id_and_user_id(form_data.file_id, user.id, db=db)\n"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The route passes the caller-derived collection_name to save_docs_to_vector_db and sets add=True whenever form_data.collection_name is present.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1694,
                  "endLine": 1706,
                  "quote": "                    result = await run_in_threadpool(\n                        save_docs_to_vector_db,\n                        request,\n                        docs=docs,\n                        collection_name=collection_name,\n                        metadata={\n                            'file_id': file.id,\n                            'name': file.filename,\n                            'hash': hash,\n                        },\n                        add=(True if form_data.collection_name else False),\n                        user=user,\n                    )"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "control": [
            {
              "statement": "A separate helper can validate collection access for a requested access type and raise 403 for denied collections, but this helper is not called in the supplied process_file path.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 2339,
                  "endLine": 2352,
                  "quote": "async def _validate_collection_access(collection_names: list[str], user, access_type: str = 'read') -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Raise 403 if the user lacks access to any of the requested collections.\n    Delegates to the shared filter_accessible_collections utility so the\n    access rules stay in one place.\n    \"\"\"\n    requested = set(collection_names)\n    allowed = await filter_accessible_collections(requested, user, access_type=access_type)\n    denied = requested - allowed\n    if denied:\n        raise HTTPException(\n            status_code=status.HTTP_403_FORBIDDEN,\n            detail=ERROR_MESSAGES.ACCESS_PROHIBITED,\n        )"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "In save_docs_to_vector_db, an existing collection causes an early return only when overwrite is false and add is false; therefore add=True permits execution to continue toward insertion into the existing collection.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1458,
                  "endLine": 1467,
                  "quote": "    try:\n        if VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.has_collection(collection_name=collection_name):\n            log.info(f'collection {collection_name} already exists')\n\n            if overwrite:\n                VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.delete_collection(collection_name=collection_name)\n                log.info(f'deleting existing collection {collection_name}')\n            elif add is False:\n                log.info(f'collection {collection_name} already exists, overwrite is False and add is False')\n                return True"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "statement": "The strongest authorization control visible in the declared route is the non-admin source-file ownership lookup; it does not compare the authenticated user with ownership or grants for the destination collection.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1559,
                  "endLine": 1563,
                  "quote": "    if user.role == 'admin':\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id(form_data.file_id, db=db)\n    else:\n        file = await Files.get_file_by_id_and_user_id(form_data.file_id, user.id, db=db)\n"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "effect": [
            {
              "statement": "The protected destination write sink inserts generated items into VECTOR_DB_CLIENT using the supplied collection_name.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
                  "startLine": 1527,
                  "endLine": 1533,
                  "quote": "        log.info(f'adding to collection {collection_name}')\n        VECTOR_DB_CLIENT.insert(\n            collection_name=collection_name,\n            items=items,\n        )\n\n        log.info(f'added {len(items)} items to collection {collection_name}')"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "condition": [
            {
              "statement": "When a collection name is supplied, the route obtains document content from the file-specific processed collection or the owned file data, without establishing permission on the supplied destination collection.",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "path": "backend/open_webui/routers/retrieval.py",
